<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>Railroads of the Tintic Mining District</name>
    <description><![CDATA[This is a comprehensive map of the Denver & Rio Grande Western's Tintic Branch over the course of its lifetime from construction in 1891 through its scrapping in 2016. The basic work was done by Don Strack as part of his Utahrails.net project; sidings, spurs, extensions, stations and industries were added by Joshua Bernhard.<br><br>The MAIN LINE and SIDINGS of the branch is DARK BLUE.<br>SPUR TRACKS are PURPLE.<br>JOINTLY-OWNED TRACK is RED.<br>UNION PACIFIC track is YELLOW.<br>CONNECTING SHORT LINES, including the Salt Lake & Utah (electric interurban) and the Eureka Hill Railway (narrow gauge) are BLACK.<br>The track currently owned by UTAH TRANSIT AUTHORITY is GREEN.<br><br>Cartographic sources include the 1891 Tintic Range Railway plat maps in the collection of Brigham Young University, the 1913 USGS topographical maps, the 1919 Beck Tunnels maps from USGS' "Geology and Ore Deposits of the Tintic District, Utah," the 1932 Chief Consolidated Mining Company claim map and the 1934 maps drawn by David DeLancey Condon.]]></description>
