      <Placemark>
        <name>1943 Line Change</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Line chnage to bypass "damaged" trestle. It was reported that the Laguna Corkscrew trestle was burned to the ground, but a 1941 Trains Magazine report shows that the new cutoff was completed while the trestle was still intact, so it is surmised that the trestle was condemned so that heavier articulated locomotives could use the route.]]></description>
