      <Placemark>
        <name>Sioux Summit
</name>
        <description>The Eureka Hill Railway reaches its highest point at the cut here.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-503-777777</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -112.0984626,39.916188,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Beck No. 1 Shaft
</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The Eureka Hill Railway was built specifically to connect Jesse Kight's Beck shafts to his smelter in Silver City.<br>Photo link: https://www.flickr.com/photos/drgw223/28108025487/in/dateposted-public/]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-503-777777</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -112.0974757,39.9408192,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Beck No. 2 Shaft
</name>
        <description><![CDATA[This was the terminus of the Eureka Hill Railway. Track reached this point in July 1908.<br>Photo link: https://collections.lib.utah.edu/details?id=523998&q=beck+mine&fd=title_t%2Csetname_s%2Ctype_t&facet_setname_s=%28dha_awg+OR+dha_alwmc+OR+dha_cbfm+OR+dha_ccc+OR+dha_cccook+dha_ccmu+OR+dha_ce+OR+dha_cp+OR+dha_crscpc+OR+dha_crvs+OR+dha_drgpl+OR+dha_ersp+OR+dha_goc+OR+dha_gmo+OR+dha_grcc+OR+dha_hill+OR+dha_jppc+OR+dha_kdfc+OR+dha_kued_trc+OR+dha_mmupc+OR+dha_obl+OR+dha_oddtwr+OR+dha_olyleg+OR+dha_rkc+OR+dha_ptfttc+OR+dha_pu+OR+dha_rucc+OR+dha_scnpp+OR+dha_sim+OR+dha_sltnc+OR+dha_scp+OR+dha_sslv+OR+dha_tpc+OR+dha_twpc+OR+dha_uplp+OR+dha_uslp+OR+dha_wehgn+OR+dha_wpabs%29]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-503-777777</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -112.0973682,39.9438477,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Utah Claim Group
</name>
        <description>The Sioux Wagon Road crossed the canyon on a massive timbered trestle in front of the tailings of these mines.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-503-777777</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -112.09975,39.9399981,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Colorado No. 1 Shaft
</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Track was completed to the Colorado No. 1 in April 1908, and the mine responded by extending their ore bin to accommodate the EHRy's hoppers.<br>Photo link: https://collections.lib.utah.edu/details?id=523972&page=5&q=eureka+utah&fd=title_t%2Csetname_s%2Ctype_t&facet_setname_s=(dha_awg+OR+dha_alwmc+OR+dha_cbfm+OR+dha_ccc+OR+dha_cccook+dha_ccmu+OR+dha_ce+OR+dha_cp+OR+dha_crscpc+OR+dha_crvs+OR+dha_drgpl+OR+dha_ersp+OR+dha_goc+OR+dha_gmo+OR+dha_grcc+OR+dha_hill+OR+dha_jppc+OR+dha_kdfc+OR+dha_kued_trc+OR+dha_mmupc+OR+dha_obl+OR+dha_oddtwr+OR+dha_olyleg+OR+dha_rkc+OR+dha_ptfttc+OR+dha_pu+OR+dha_rucc+OR+dha_scnpp+OR+dha_sim+OR+dha_sltnc+OR+dha_scp+OR+dha_sslv+OR+dha_tpc+OR+dha_twpc+OR+dha_uplp+OR+dha_uslp+OR+dha_wehgn+OR+dha_wpabs)]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-503-777777</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -112.0952091,39.9365287,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Colorado No. 1 Spur
</name>
        <description><![CDATA[A brick warehouse and wood loading dock were constructed on this spur.<br>Photo link: https://www.flickr.com/photos/drgw223/28063102317/in/dateposted-public/]]></description>
