      <Placemark>
        <name>York Station
</name>
        <description><![CDATA[The Utah Southern ended construction here for several years before continuing on to Milford, and a railroad town was constructed as the terminus. This was the closest railhead to the Tintic mountains and was the location where ore was loaded onto the trains until the Salt Lake & Western was built on the west side of the Tintic Mountains.<br>Location determined by a map approved by the General Land Office in 1875 provided by Don Strack.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-503-DB4436</styleUrl>
