      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[Leamington Cutoff (SPLA&SL)
]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[The Leamington Cutoff was a modernized connection to Salt Lake City built by the Oregon Short Line. It was later purchased by the SPLA&SL that ran from Los Angeles to Salt Lake City. It replaced the original Salt lake & Western route from Lehi when completed in June 1903.]]></description>
