        <name><![CDATA[Salt Lake & Mercur interchange
]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[The Salt Lake & Mercur, a shay-powered mining railroad that ran from the SL&W to the town of Mercur, interchanged here. The concrete foundations of an unknown building prompted the USGS to mark this location as "Ruin." It was most likely related to the railroad, since it is oriented exactly parallel to the grade.]]></description>
